  "rules_year": 2026,
  "notes": "medicaid_expansion: state covers adults to adult_limit_fpl of the federal poverty line (income test only, no asset test). Non-expansion: childless adults generally ineligible; below 100% FPL there is no marketplace credit (coverage gap). WI covers adults to 100% FPL without the ACA expansion and is treated as non-expansion.",
  "community_engagement": {
    "source_url": "https://www.medicaid.gov/federal-policy-guidance/downloads/cib12082025.pdf",
    "start_year": 2027,
    "hours_per_month": 80,
    "min_age": 19,
    "max_age_exclusive": 65,
    "summary": "Expansion adults 19-64 must show 80 hrs/month of work, community service, a work program or half-time school (or monthly income of at least 80 x federal minimum wage) to stay on Medicaid. Those who fail and would otherwise qualify are also barred from marketplace premium tax credits. States may get a good-faith delay to no later than 2028-12-31."
